{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01TTKANTXExzHy1AVk9QXk1u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q9 — What logic belongs in orchestrator vs LLM?**\n\n**Key content:**\n\n- **Orchestrator owns (deterministic/policy):** loop control (`max_iterations`, wall-clock timeout), tool dispatch + JSON schema validation, retry/backoff, budget enforcement, HITL gates before irreversible actions, state persistence, security allowlists\n- **LLM owns (stochastic/reasoning):** goal decomposition, tool selection, intermediate ReAct reasoning, answer synthesis, ambiguity resolution\n- **Concrete example:** LangGraph support-ticket agent — the graph enforces limits and `interrupt_before(\"escalate\")` HITL; the LLM gets a clean ReAct prompt for reasoning only\n- **Anti-pattern called out explicitly:** putting routing conditionals (`\"if severity > 3, escalate\"`) in the prompt — fragile, expensive, unjailbreakable\n- **Pitfalls:** prompt-based routing, no orchestrator loop limit, in-prompt tool validation\n- **Cross-links:** Q8 (full architecture), Q10 (safe loop design), Q14 (infinite loop detection)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":275,"cache_read_input_tokens":62186,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":275,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3872912b-0ad6-4912-be70-71dd31431c26","uuid":"8a7a5634-6407-47ee-9459-e3c6757333e9"}
